# `vercel --prod` uploads the working tree, and it does not read .gitignore.
# Anything git ignores can still ship to a deployment unless it is named here —
# which is how a local test journal ended up being served from production.
#
# A push to main deploys from git and only carries committed files, so this
# file is the belt to that braces. Deploy from git; keep this correct anyway.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Ingested telemetry and the journal are a plant's own records, written at
# runtime on a box with a disk. They are never part of a build.
data/

# Test output, contract build artifacts, and the suites themselves. None of it
# runs in production and the videos are megabytes.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright-mcp/
artifacts/
cache/
e2e/
test/
docs/*.webm
docs/page@*.webm

.vercel
.git

submission/
